1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.233
Welcome to Building Your Own Database
Agent, built

2
00:00:03.233 --> 00:00:05.400
in partnership with Microsoft.

3
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:09.033
In this course, you'll learn
how LLMs can interact with structured

4
00:00:09.033 --> 00:00:12.700
data like tabular data or SQL databases.

5
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.800
This is very useful when you're building
a system to answer questions

6
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:21.000
using data sources with tables of data,
rather than needing to find

7
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.400
maybe an analyst to translate a question
to a SQL database query,

8
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:29.133
you see how a database agents
can automatically

9
00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:32.700
input a question
and generate a sequence of actions.

10
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:36.000
This function calls to retrieve
the relevant data.

11
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:41.600
Specifically, in this course,
you learn how to build your own AI agent

12
00:00:41.733 --> 00:00:45.333
to interact with tabular data
and SQL databases.

13
00:00:45.833 --> 00:00:49.400
Along the way, you'll learn about
some of the key building blocks for agents

14
00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:52.800
and will be using the LangChain agents
framework.

15
00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:54.200
I'm delighted that our

16
00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:57.633
instructor for this course is Adrian
Gonzalez Sanchez.

17
00:00:58.233 --> 00:01:03.000
He is a data AI specialist at Microsoft,
teaches at the University level,

18
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.900
and is also author of the Azure OpenAI
O'Reilly book.

19
00:01:07.733 --> 00:01:09.400
Thanks, Andrew.

20
00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.133
I'm very excited to be here.

21
00:01:11.133 --> 00:01:15.633
In this course, you will learn
how to deploy LLMs to build your AI agent.

22
00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:19.133
Implement RAG with tabular data.

23
00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:22.133
Develop your own database agent.

24
00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:24.700
Build a function calling system,

25
00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:28.633
integrate Azure OpenAI assistance
API.

26
00:01:28.633 --> 00:01:33.333
You'll go through these concepts using
the Azure OpenAI service and LangChain.

27
00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:37.600
Although we'll be using a database agent
as a running example,

28
00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:42.100
these components are useful
for building any other agents as well.

29
00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:46.833
So database agents are an exciting
breakthrough for how we analyze data,

30
00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:50.300
is letting people interact
with complex datasets

31
00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:53.533
without needing to learn
query languages like SQL,

32
00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.800
so that you can have an LLM
perform requests to a database for you,

33
00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:02.633
regardless of the database
provider, data model, or type language.

34
00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:06.933
Using an LLM as an extraction layer
on top of the database

35
00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:10.900
is one of the new frontiers
for data democratization

36
00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:14.200
within many companies,
and perhaps you could bring this

37
00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:18.100
to fruition for your company
or for applications you're working on.

38
00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:20.500
I mean, how exciting is that?

39
00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:25.200
Further, I see agents as a rapidly
growing category with in terms of AI,

40
00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:30.033
and you also learn about key components
to agents and best practices

41
00:02:30.033 --> 00:02:33.300
for assembling these components
into draw this system.

42
00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:37.600
Many people have worked to create
this course from the Microsoft side

43
00:02:37.633 --> 00:02:42.633
I'd like to thank Jorge
Garcia Ximenez, Agustine SantaMaria,

44
00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:47.600
Arancha Diez Garcia and Xiaopeng Li.
From DeepLearning.AI,

45
00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:51.400
Diala Ezzeddine also contributed
to this course.

46
00:02:51.733 --> 00:02:55.300
In the first lesson,
you will start building your first AI agent

47
00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:56.900
with the Azure OpenAI service.

48
00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:01.400
So let's
go on to the next video to get started.

